This repository's own files (the mac/ orchestrator, the tools, the tests, the launchd job and the documents) are
MIT, see LICENSE.

patches/glm-one-mac-vision-v1.0.4.patch is a change set to TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold,
Apache License 2.0, copyright the TensorFold contributors) and is distributed under the Apache License 2.0 like the
code it modifies (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). `python3 -m mac build` applies it on top of TensorFold at the pinned
commit. Its image resampler follows Pillow's Resample.c (MIT-CMU licence, the Pillow authors) and its erf follows
FreeBSD's msun (Sun Microsystems' permissive notice); both are reimplemented, not copied, to match their results.

The checkpoint this recipe serves, TensorFold/GLM-5.3-Flash-MLX-4bit-MTP, is a conversion of Z.AI's GLM-5.3-Flash
and carries the MIT licence (copyright Z.AI Co., Ltd); the recipe downloads it from Hugging Face and does not
redistribute weights. tests/images/zai-logo.png is the logo shipped in that checkpoint's repository.

The quality suite and decode ruler are the Spark recipe's (BobClawblaw/qwen38-flashnext-int4mixed-2x-dgx-sparks),
cloned at a pinned commit under .external/ and run there; nothing of them is copied into this tree. tools/
vision_reference.py and tools/vision_noise.py import TensorFold 0.6.6 and mlx-vlm (MIT) from a separate venv, as
references only.
